<title>FRANCE: French budget deficit to end July 273.6 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French budget deficit to end July 273.6 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French budget deficit at end July stood at 273.6 billion francs, down 8.5 billion francs from a deficit of 282.1 billion francs a year earlier, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cumulative net tax receipts stood at 784.0 billion francs at end July, up 5.6 percent from 742.2 billion francs for the same period a year earlier, the ministry said.</p>
<p>General budget spending was up 2.8 percent at end July at 945.9 billion francs, over the same period a year earlier.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown of budget receipts: (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1996 year forecast):</p>
<p> REVENUES			end Jul 96  Jul 95  pct	1996</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		 784.0    742.2   5.6    1,401.1</p>
<p>  of which: -- income tax     181.2    177.5   2.1	310.1</p>
<p>  -- net company tax	     78.6     64.9  21.1	131.6</p>
<p>  -- petrol duties		 83.4     80.4   3.7	148.5</p>
<p>  -- net Value Added Tax	354.1    324.6   9.1	634.7</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		 86.7     94.8  -8.5	176.2</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		  61.0     69.8 -12.6	132.4</p>
<p> Local authority, EU charges -146.9   -136.3   7.8     -252.5</p>
<p> General budget receipts	698.1    675.7   3.3    1,281.0</p>
<p> SPENDING			end Jun 96  Jun 95  pct</p>
<p> Ordinary civil spending	776.1    756.4   2.6</p>
<p> of which debt		    138.0    137.0   0.7</p>
<p> Capital civil spending	  55.8     52.6   6.1</p>
<p> Ordinary military spending    64.6     64.5   0.2</p>
<p> Capital military spending     49.4     46.3   6.7</p>
<p> TOTAL BUDGET SPENDING	  945.9    919.8   2.8</p>
<p>BALANCE</p>
<p> Total net spending	     945.9    919.8   2.8</p>
<p> Total net receipts	     738.2    709.2   4.1</p>
<p> General budget deficit	-207.7   -210.6</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts    -65.9    -71.5</p>
<p> TOTAL CENTRAL GOVT DEFICIT  -273.6   -282.1</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5542</p>
</text>
